---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import WhatsAppFloat from '../components/WhatsAppFloat.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | DraftToDesign"
  description="DraftToDesign terms of service: how our design services work, pricing, revisions, delivery, and your responsibilities as a client."
>
  <Header slot="header" />
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-brand-900 mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-8">Last updated: September 25, 2026</p>
    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none text-slate-600 leading-relaxed space-y-5">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of drafttodesign.com and our design services.
        By requesting a quote or ordering services, you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Our services</h2>
      <p>
        DraftToDesign provides remote <strong>design and visualization services
        only</strong>: 2D floor plans, architectural drafting, 3D modeling,
        photorealistic 3D rendering, interior design concepts, and exterior/landscaping
        concepts. All work is delivered digitally.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> provide building permit submission sets, structural
        engineering, stamped or sealed drawings, or construction documentation. Our
        deliverables are design tools for planning, presentation, and contractor
        bidding, not legal construction documents.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Quotes and pricing</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Prices shown on our website are starting prices. Every project receives a fixed written quote before work begins.</li>
        <li>A quote is valid for 30 days from the date it is issued.</li>
        <li>The quoted price covers the agreed scope only. Additional views, rooms, or major scope changes are quoted separately.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Revisions</h2>
      <p>
        Every project includes <strong>two revision rounds</strong> at no extra charge.
        A revision round means a consolidated list of changes submitted at one time.
        Change requests beyond the included rounds, or changes that alter the project
        scope, may incur additional fees quoted in advance.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Delivery</h2>
      <p>
        Delivery timelines stated on our website or in your quote are estimates based
        on our current workload. We communicate proactively if a timeline shifts.
        Delivery times assume you provide required inputs (plans, measurements,
        reference images) promptly; delays on your side extend the timeline accordingly.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Provide accurate measurements, plans, and project requirements.</li>
        <li>Confirm that you have the rights to any reference materials you share.</li>
        <li>Review deliverables promptly and submit revision requests as consolidated lists.</li>
        <li>Verify our drawings and designs with your local contractor, engineer, or authority before construction. Our work does not replace professional site verification.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Payment terms are agreed in writing before work starts. For most projects we
        require a deposit to begin, with the balance due on final delivery. Source
        files remain our property until the project is paid in full.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Once paid in full, you receive full rights to use the final deliverables for
        your project, including presentations, listings, and construction planning.
        We may display completed work in our portfolio unless you request otherwise
        in writing before delivery.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Cancellations and refunds</h2>
      <p>
        You may cancel a project before work begins for a full refund of any deposit.
        Once work has started, the deposit is non-refundable, and you will be billed
        for work completed to the cancellation date. If we cannot deliver as agreed,
        you are entitled to a refund for the undelivered portion.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        Our liability is limited to the amount you paid for the project in question.
        We are not liable for construction costs, delays, or decisions made based on
        our design deliverables. Always verify designs with qualified local
        professionals before building.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms occasionally. The version in effect when you order
        applies to your project.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-900 pt-4">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Reach us via our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
        or WhatsApp at <a href="https://wa.me/923044719600">+92 304 4719600</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer slot="footer" />
  <WhatsAppFloat />
</BaseLayout>
